# Use TavariCheckbox for all checkboxes

In this codebase, **plain `<input type="checkbox">` is often invisible** in the Tavari dashboard (global input styles, Electron/WebView, etc.).

## React (dashboard, modules, settings)

**Always** use `TavariCheckbox` from `src/components/UI/TavariCheckbox.jsx`.

```jsx
import TavariCheckbox from '../../components/UI/TavariCheckbox';

<TavariCheckbox
  id="unique-id"
  checked={checked}
  onChange={(next) => setChecked(next)}
  label="Option label"
/>
```

- Do **not** add raw `<input type="checkbox">` in React screens/components.
- Prefer default `appearance="custom"` (styled teal box + checkmark).
- Use `appearance="native"` only when a deliberate OS-native control is required.

## Non-React surfaces (e.g. `public/task-manager-kiosk/`)

Vanilla HTML cannot import the React component. Use the **same visual pattern**:

- Hidden input: `class="tavari-checkbox-input …"`
- Visible box: `<span class="tavari-checkbox-box">`
- Wrapper: `<label class="tavari-checkbox">`
- Helper: `renderTavariCheckboxHtml()` in `public/task-manager-kiosk/app.es5.js`
- Styles live in `public/task-manager-kiosk/index.html` (`.tavari-checkbox*`)

Do **not** rely on unstyled native checkboxes in kiosk HTML.

## Global CSS

Avoid `input { width: 100% }` without excluding checkboxes. Prefer `input:not([type="checkbox"]), textarea { … }`.
